{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And Moses heard, and fell upon his face.</b> He did not include Aaron in this, so as to say 'and they fell,' and this was because of his exceeding humility and self-discipline, since the core of the dispute was over Aaron's priesthood. But Moses saw his brother's disgrace and had pity on his honor, and therefore he alone fell upon his face. And perhaps in this falling on the face Moses punished Korah and all his assembly, and from here Rabbi Eliezer learned to punish Rabban Gamliel by falling on the face, as is mentioned at the end of the chapter HaZahav." "<b>And it is known</b> to every discerning person that תחנה (supplication) belongs to the attribute of Justice and to the left hand, for it is the hand fitting for this. And a full verse states it (Psalms 10): ״אליך ה' אקרא ואל אדני אתחנן״, and it is written (Job 8): ״אם אתה תשחר אל אל ואל שדי תתחנן״, and so Moses mentioned (Deuteronomy 3): ״ואתחנן אל ה'״, and he immediately juxtaposed אדני, in which is mercy. And so Solomon mentioned in his prayer (I Kings 8): ״ויהיו דברי אלה אשר התחננתי לפני ה'״ — he did not say 'to HaShem' but 'before HaShem,' in the manner of (Numbers 15): ״וחטאתם לפני ה' על שגגתם״, and this is clear." "<b>And in the Midrash:</b> 'And Moses heard, and fell upon his face' — a parable: to a king's son who sinned against his father, and his friend interceded for him once, twice, and three times. When he sinned a fourth time, the king's friend's hands grew slack. He said: how many times will I trouble the king? So too Moses said thus: they sinned with the calf — (Exodus 32) ״ויחל משה״; with the complainers — (Numbers 11) ״ויתפלל משה״; with the spies — (ibid. 14) ״ויאמר משה אל ה' ושמעו מצרים״; at the dispute of Korah his hands grew slack. He said: how many times am I troubling the Place? Therefore: ״ויפול על פניו״."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {1 "The verse cited as Psalms 10 is actually Psalms 38:15 (אליך ה' אקרא ואל אדני אתחנן); the chapter number appears corrupt. Job 8 is also uncertain: the cited phrase 'אם אתה תשחר אל אל ואל שדי תתחנן' does not match Job 8 but combines language from Job 8:5 and Job 22:26–27."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:32:58.763294501Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}